1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,628
Welcome to Tense Lab!

2
00:00:01,628 --> 00:00:07,775
Today, we are going to make the twelve English tenses easier to understand and remember.

3
00:00:07,775 --> 00:00:12,734
Let us begin with the three time zones: past, present, and future.

4
00:00:12,734 --> 00:00:13,996
First, simple tenses.

5
00:00:13,996 --> 00:00:16,072
Think of the main action.

6
00:00:16,072 --> 00:00:16,927
She plays.

7
00:00:16,927 --> 00:00:17,781
She played.

8
00:00:17,781 --> 00:00:19,043
She will play.

9
00:00:19,043 --> 00:00:20,305
Next, continuous tenses.

10
00:00:20,305 --> 00:00:26,452
Look for a form of the verb BE, followed by a verb ending in I-N-G.

11
00:00:26,452 --> 00:00:27,714
She is playing.

12
00:00:27,714 --> 00:00:28,976
She was playing.

13
00:00:28,976 --> 00:00:30,645
She will be playing.

14
00:00:30,645 --> 00:00:31,907
Now, perfect tenses.

15
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:37,240
Look for HAVE, HAS, HAD, or WILL HAVE, followed by a past participle.

16
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:38,502
She has played.

17
00:00:38,502 --> 00:00:39,764
She had played.

18
00:00:39,764 --> 00:00:41,433
She will have played.

19
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:43,102
Finally, perfect continuous tenses.

20
00:00:43,102 --> 00:00:49,656
Look for a form of HAVE, followed by BEEN, followed by a verb ending in I-N-G.

21
00:00:49,656 --> 00:00:51,325
She has been playing.

22
00:00:51,325 --> 00:00:52,994
She had been playing.

23
00:00:52,994 --> 00:00:55,070
She will have been playing.

24
00:00:55,070 --> 00:01:01,250
Here is an important reminder: the I-N-G ending alone does not identify a continuous tense.

25
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,733
Look for the helping verb, too.

26
00:01:03,733 --> 00:01:05,842
Ready for a quick challenge?

27
00:01:05,842 --> 00:01:09,579
Which sentence is in the present perfect continuous tense?

28
00:01:09,579 --> 00:01:12,094
Option A: She plays every day.

29
00:01:12,094 --> 00:01:14,610
Option B: She has played today.

30
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:18,347
Option C: She has been playing for an hour.

31
00:01:18,347 --> 00:01:19,976
The answer is C!

32
00:01:19,976 --> 00:01:22,052
You are ready to practise.

33
00:01:22,052 --> 00:01:28,199
Choose a tense, test your understanding, and build your confidence one question at a time.

34
00:01:28,199 --> 00:01:29,868
Welcome to Tense Lab.

35
00:01:29,868 --> 00:01:31,089
Let us begin!

